Apply the Galilean rules – to the light ray: $\begin{aligned}
x'&=x-vt=(c-v)t,\\
t'&=t.\end{aligned}$ The primed observer would therefore infer $x'=(c-v)t',$ so right-moving light would have speed $c-v$. For a left-moving ray $x=-ct$, $x'=-(c+v)t',$ whose speed has magnitude $c+v$.

